ltivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: Availability or class schedule: \u2022 Options of one or two days per week are available. \u2022 Clinical rotations are 8 weeks in length. Responsibilities \u2022 Include working with a small group of students in the clinical setting assisting with providing patient care. \u2022 Facilitating communication with the agency staff. \u2022 Assisting students with communication to other healthcare providers, patients, and families. \u2022 Ensuring facility documentation is completed by the student. \u2022 Supervising medication administration and completion of skills. \u2022 Grading student work. \u2022 Assisting with on-campus skills checkoffs and simulation. Required Qualifications: \u2022 BSN \u2022 Minimum of two-year\u2019s experience in the nursing field \u2022 RN licensed in Kansas \u2022 Demonstrated dedication to developing inclusive teaching practices that engage all learners. \u2022 RN licensed in Kansas \u2022 Official educational transcripts are required at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: MSN or working on MSN Special Instructions to Applicants: Questions pertaining to this position may be directed to Dr. Debbie Isaacson, debbie.isaacson@washburn.edu . Applications will be reviewed as received and based on department need. Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) bff6ae90 Last Name (required) 7f09f585 Email (required) 7e547a2e Job Alert e468da36 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Nursing School of Nursing Categories Nursing Nursing Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Invol