ions for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 25623aa9 Last Name (required) 06af6ffb Email (required) 4b59b64f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking \u201cI Accept\u201d or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"}, "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/adjunct-school-of-law-topeka-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Adjunct (School of Law)", "description": "Adjunct (School of Law) - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Adjunct (School of Law) School of Law Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Adjunct (School of Law) School of Law Adjunct Position Title: Adjunct (School of Law) Department: School of Law Campus Location: Washburn University Application Deadline: Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Position Summary: Washburn University School of Law invites applications for an adjunct instructor to teach a variety of courses beginning in the 2026-2027 academic year. Each selected candidate will have a demonstrated commitment to pursuing teaching excellence at Washburn University, including a dedication to developing teaching practices that engage students from all backgrounds. The School of Law moved into its new, state-of-the-art building in July 2023. The building features classrooms equipped with up-to-date recording technology, including closed captioning; a green room recording studio; and beautiful trial and appellate courtrooms. The Washburn campus is located blocks from the historic state capitol. Topeka features affordable housing; beautiful, historic neighborhoods with well-maintained parks; and a nationally recognized public library. It is also the home of the Brown v. Board of Education National Historical Site. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: \u2022 Fulfill teaching expectations associated with an adjunct instructor appointment. Required Qualifications: \u2022 JD degree from an ABA-approved law school. \u2022 Demonstrated interest in teaching. \u2022 Dedication to developing teaching practices that engage students from all backgrounds. \u2022 Official educational transcripts required at time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Record of teaching. Special Instructions to Applicants: \u2022 Interested candidates should submit their resume, cover letter, and the names/addresses/phone numbers of three professional references through the Washburn University job portal. \u2022 If you have questions about the position, please contact Emily Grant, Associate Dean of Academic Affairs, at emily.grant@washburn.edu . Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) dd73434b Last Name (required) c51ed366 Email (required) b318dc36 Job Alert dcd1a868 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Law School of Law Categories Law, Legal Studies, Forensics Law, Legal Studies, Forensics Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Washburn University\u2019s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) a6bd60cc Last Name (required) f8b23a03 Email (required) 8e5853d3 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking \u201cI Accept\u201d or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"}, "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/anthropology-special-project-lab-assistant-topeka-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Anthropology Special Project Lab Assistant", "description": "Anthropology Special Project Lab Assistant - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Anthropology Special Project Lab Assistant Forensic Center Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Anthropology Special Project Lab Assistant Forensic Center Staff Temporary Position Title: Anthropology Special Project Lab Assistant Department: FC Anthropology Advertised Pay: $15.00/hr Campus Location: Washburn University Application Review: Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Position Summary: Work with Anthropology/WU-FARU faculty and staff to facilitate the analysis and cataloguing of archaeological collections and human remains. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: \u2022 Prepare and organize material to be analyzed \u2022 Pack and sort materials \u2022 Maintain data records using Microsoft Office Suite (e.g., Word, Excel, PowerPoint) \u2022 Bend, lift, and move archaeological materials contained in boxes/shelves to and from workstations. Required Qualifications: \u2022 Grade of B or better in AN316 Forensic Anthropology. \u2022 Proficiency with Microsoft Word and Excel. \u2022 Ability to maintain discretion and confidentiality. Physical Requirements: \u2022 Ability to bend, move, and lift materials weighing up to 30 pounds. \u2022 Capacity to use a ladder and/or step stool and stand for long periods of time (~7-8 hours). \u2022 Reliable transportation to and from job location during work periods. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Completion of AN327 Fragmentary Human Osteology (grade B or above) and/or volunteer hours with the WU-FARU (minimum of 10 hours). \u2022 Detail-oriented with effective time management and organizational skills. \u2022 Demonstrated effective communication skills with the ability to work effectively on a team. Hourly, Part-time, Temporary Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) 751c5f7d Last Name (required) 385d2290 Email (required) 0430ee03 Job Alert db74721e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Forensic Center Forensic Center Categories Clinical Lab Assistants Clinical Lab Assistants Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Washburn University\u2019s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 52d9dca8 Last Name (required) ab84a96b Email (required) 2c199719 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking \u201cI Accept\u201d or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"}, "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/application-analyst-topeka-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Application Analyst", "description": "Application Analyst - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Application Analyst Information Technology Services Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Application Analyst Information Technology Services Staff Full-time Position Title: Application Analyst Department: Information Technology Services Advertised Pay: Lower $70,000's Campus Location: Washburn University Application Review: Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Position Summary: The Application Analyst is responsible for providing operational support for University business applications and to the users of those applications. This includes development, testing, troubleshooting, and ongoing support of the chosen software system (currently Ellucian Banner) and related/partner applications as well as the creation and support of various business process solutions, operational reports, and system integrations. This position works closely with both ITS and functional areas to identify, analyze, and meet the business needs of the University using available technologies. The Application Analyst is responsible for and assigned to primarily support one of the following areas: \u2022 Admissions Office in its use of Admissions and Enrollment Management software modules. \u2022 Financial Aid Office in its use of Financial Aid software modules. \u2022 Registrar Office and the Student software module and the areas of campus that use it. \u2022 Vice President of Administration and Treasurer (shared responsibility for Human Resources, Payroll, Purchasing, Budget, and Finance) functions in the appropriate software. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: \u2022 Interact with functional users via telephone, email, and meetings to provide end-user support for the administrative information systems software. \u2022 Examine job functions and analyze the security needs of individuals authorized by area heads to access the administrative information software. Recommend the appropriate security classes to the appropriate staff. \u2022 Communicate with other Application Analysts, and analyze the impact of assigned modules on other areas of the administrative information system software to make configuration decisions providing for non-problematic integration of modules. \u2022 Monitor patches and upgrades of the administrative information systems software and other integrated software, informing areas of needed patches/upgrades to keep the modules current and reliable. \u2022 Analyze data integrity issues and determine appropriate steps to clean up data to maintain the integrity of the system. \u2022 Develop scenarios in test mode to replicate problems/errors and design possible solutions through the testing of alternatives. \u2022 Test/troubleshoot software integrated with the administrative information systems software. \u2022 Collaborate with Systems Administrator staff, the Database Administrator, and/or vendors to install, update, and configure partner applications and integrations to ensure software meets the needs of the functional areas. \u2022 Collaborate with appropriate staff to make necessary changes to the production database after appropriate testing and sign-off from the appropriate area head. \u2022 Document application services processes to establish and modify backup procedures for use by other Application Analysts. \u2022 Consult listservs, release guides and vendor online support, and communicate with other educational institutions to identify and research solutions to problems in administrative information systems software. \u2022 Research features of future versions of administrative information systems software to assess their impact on functionality, including self-service, to plan for future implementation. Provide high-level summaries of new features to the supervisor for making decisions about future projects. \u2022 Develop specifications for queries/reports and write corresponding SQL scripts to generate queries/reports/extracts. Check the output for reasonableness. \u2022 Document query/report criteria and reflect report criteria with the report through meaningful titles and column headings or other annotations where necessary. \u2022 Collaborate with other Application Analysts and Strategic Analysis, Research and Reporting (SARR) to standardize data definitions and minimize duplication of code. \u2022 Analyze the needs of functional users, and develop and document applications/solutions to meet these needs. \u2022 Together with ITS staff, create testing scenarios for the applications being implemented. \u2022 Test to see if applications/solutions meet the required specifications. \u2022 Collaborate with other Application Analysts to develop reference materials for the application services software. \u2022 Inform staff on the technical usage of modules in the administrative information systems software. \u2022 Provide backup training for other Application Analysts on the general navigation of administrative information systems software. \u2022 Provide backup for other Application Analysts and the department\u2019s supervisor tasks. \u2022 Serve as an Information Technology Services representative on project teams as assigned. \u2022 Document issues and known solutions using ticket-tracking software. \u2022 Perform additional job-related duties as assigned or as appropriate. \u2022 In addition, the application analyst may be assigned the responsibility to support one or more of the following tools, dependent on the specific area of focus or required tool: o Dynamic Forms o Ellucian Experience o AppEnhancer (Imaging) o Technolutions Slate o Argos o IntelleCheck o formFusion o Other Systems yet to be adopted \u2022 Performs additional job-related duties as assigned or as appropriate. Required Qualifications: \u2022 A post-secondary degree in CIS or CS and one year of experience creating SQL database queries using TOAD, Access, SQL Developer, Brio/Hyperion or any similar query tool; OR a combination of relevant post-secondary education and closely related information technology work experience equivalent to at least two years and one year of experience creating SQL database queries using TOAD, Access, SQL Developer, Brio/Hyperion or any similar query tool. \u2022 Demonstrated effective interpersonal and communication skills. \u2022 Proven effective problem-solving and analytical skills. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with any of the following: \u2022 Accounting/Payroll \u2022 Travel and expense management systems \u2022 PL/SQL coding \u2022 Integrated database information systems \u2022 Student Information Systems (SIS) and/or financial aid systems \u2022 Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) systems \u2022 Slate integration \u2022 Customer Relationship Management (CRM) systems \u2022 Finance, Budgeting, and/or Human Resource systems \u2022 Enterprise Content Management (ECM) systems \u2022 Institutional research and/or operational reporting \u2022 Operational data store and/or data warehouses \u2022 Workflow, automation, electronic forms, scanning/imaging \u2022 Ellucian Higher Education (Banner) software \u2022 Technolutions Slate \u2022 Ellucian Degree Works \u2022 Ellucian Experience \u2022 Ellucian Ethos \u2022 Automic \u2022 Evisions MAPS (Argos, FormFusion, IntelleCheck) software \u2022 Dynamic Forms \u2022 OpenText ApplicationXtender \u2022 ScholarshipUniverse \u2022 Other Higher Education software Exempt, Full time, Mon-Fri, 8am-5pm Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) d3d3cbd2 Last Name (required) 9033ec04 Email (required) 7bf77bb2 Job Alert fcd75e7b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Information Technology Services Information Technology Services Categories Information Technology Services Information Technology Services Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Washburn University\u2019s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. University Counselor / Campus Advocate (Two positions) Counseling Washburn University is accepting applications to hire two University Counselor / Campus Advocate positions. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) c3248ba2 Last Name (required) 826798b4 Email (required) 4d5c4a6d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking \u201cI Accept\u201d or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"}, "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/assistant-director-campus-visit-experience-topeka-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Director, Campus Visit Experience", "description": "Assistant Director, Campus Visit Experience - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Assistant Director, Campus Visit Experience Admissions Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant Director, Campus Visit Experience Admissions Staff Full-time Position Title: Assistant Director, Campus Visit Experience Department: Undergraduate Recruit & Admissions Advertised Pay: Low to Mid $50,000's Campus Location: Washburn University Application Review: Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Position Summary: This position contributes to undergraduate new student recruitment at Washburn by leading the campus visit experience, including personalized campus visits, group visits, and recruitment events. The Assistant Director, Campus Visit Experience supervises the Campus Visit Experience staff and manages the Student Ambassador program. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: \u2022 Serve as the supervising contact for all Undergraduate Recruitment and Admissions campus visitors and will lead and manage the planning and execution of all undergraduate new student recruitment events and the personalized campus visits for prospective students and their parents/guests. \u2022 Supervise, support, and manage assigned staff to maximize employee performance and facilitate professional growth. Recruit, hire, train, schedule, and evaluate the performance and effectiveness of assigned staff. Conduct meetings and performance reviews with assigned staff to provide appropriate feedback and professional development opportunities to ensure job expectations are understood and met, and encourage staff to work toward individual and department goals. Work to maintain a healthy and fair work environment by promoting and exercising teamwork and collaboration. \u2022 Ensure assigned staff receive training, understand, and make effective contributions to all areas of the campus visit experience and the new student recruitment process through an informative, fun, and engaging visit experience. \u2022 Serve as the lead point of contact for the Washburn community in the collaborative planning, scheduling, and execution of undergraduate recruitment events, group visits, and personalized campus visits. Serve as the lead point of contact for high school, community college, and community personnel to collaboratively bring prospective students to Washburn for the campus visit experience. \u2022 Alongside Enrollment Management Strategic Marketing and Communications, collaboratively manage all communications regarding the campus visit experience, ensuring timely and informative communications are sent to visitors about their campus visit experiences. \u2022 Work collaboratively with appropriate staff to ensure timely and accurate marketing and promotion of and communication for new student recruitment campus visit events. \u2022 Manage and approve work schedules and timesheets for assigned staff. \u2022 Collect, analyze, interpret, and assess data from all aspects of the campus visit experience, using data to strategically inform future efforts and direction. \u2022 Attend conferences and other training programs/events regarding higher education leadership, new student recruitment, and the campus visit experience to improve management ability, identify best practices, and learn new strategies to ensure a fun, engaging, and effective student ambassador program and campus visit experience. \u2022 Participate in unit and department meetings, training opportunities, and other appropriate professional development. \u2022 Remain aware of and competent in the use of emerging recruitment and enrollment technologies. \u2022 Perform additional job-related duties as assigned or as appropriate. Required Qualifications: \u2022 Bachelor\u2019s degree. \u2022 Two years of experience in collegiate recruitment, admissions, sales, collegiate activities, or other related areas. \u2022 Experience in event management, facilitation, or related work. \u2022 Demonstrated effective interpersonal and communication skills. \u2022 Ability to work effectively independently and within a team construct. \u2022 Proven ability and commitment to establishing and maintaining effective professional relationships, including underrepresented student populations. \u2022 Proven ability to organize and manage multiple tasks in a fast-paced environment with many interruptions while adhering to deadlines. \u2022 Demonstrated capacity to effectively use Windows operating software and Microsoft Office products. \u2022 Valid driver's license with an acceptable driving record under Washburn's standards. Physical Requirements: \u2022 Ability to handle and maneuver objects weighing up to 25 pounds. \u2022 Ability to drive golf cart-type vehicles around campus. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Experience in a supervisory role. \u2022 Washburn University Alumni. Exempt, Full-time, Mon-Fri, 8am-5pm Background check and driving history are required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) 28a7e531 Last Name (required) 784a2c1a Email (required) 0c9fd690 Job Alert c9ec50d8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Admissions Admissions Categories Academic Advising, Student Success/Retention Academic Advising, Student Success/Retention Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Washburn University\u2019s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 2a53d8ad Last Name (required) 1bc00228 Email (required) bc6cc20a Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking \u201cI Accept\u201d or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"}, "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/assistant-general-counsel-topeka-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant General Counsel", "description": "Assistant General Counsel - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Assistant General Counsel President Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant General Counsel President Staff Full-time Position Title: Assistant General Counsel Department: General Counsel Advertised Pay: Competitive Campus Location: Washburn University Application Review: Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Position Summary: This position reports directly to the General Counsel and Secretary to the Board of Regents and assists with providing comprehensive legal advice and counsel to senior academic and administrative leaders; contracts review, legal research, analysis, and writing; and compliance review, assessment, and recommendations. Additional specific areas of responsibility will be determined based on Washburn needs and in conjunction with professional experience. This position provides proactive, customer-service oriented legal support and guidance to clients across the campus community. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: \u2022 Proactively advise a wide range of Washburn leaders on multifaceted matters, including investigations, facility use agreements, real estate, affiliation agreements, public records, federal and state regulations, academic and student affairs, regulatory compliance, intellectual property, labor and employment, and risk management. \u2022 Review, draft, negotiate, and manage contracts, affiliation agreements, and other agreements on behalf of Washburn. \u2022 Administer and maintain Washburn\u2019s contract management system, including workflow, development, user support, training, and implementation of process improvements designed to increase efficiency and transparency. \u2022 Manage legal projects and research as assigned and ensure timely completion and adherence to legal standards. \u2022 Prepare correspondence, reports, policies, and other legal documents as needed as part of legal projects and as assigned. \u2022 Research legal and operations issues as assigned and provide recommendations to support institutional decision-making, policy development, and risk management efforts. \u2022 Administer Washburn\u2019s open records management system and coordinate responses to requests under the Kansas Open Records Act (KORA). Delegate any such tasks as appropriate, managing to ensure timeliness and adherence to laws. \u2022 Assist in directing and supervising legal interns, including assigning work, training and mentorship, and reviewing work product. \u2022 Work with unit leaders to review and assess Washburn programs, policies, regulations, and procedures; advise as to the level of compliance and any needed changes. \u2022 Respond to questions and requests for assistance with compliance and legal issues, advising with consideration of legal and other relevant factors to offer practical solutions. \u2022 Develop and conduct legal and compliance education sessions for faculty and staff as needed. \u2022 Provide legal advice to the Board of Regents in the absence of the General Counsel and attend Board of Regents meetings. \u2022 Maintain confidentiality regarding sensitive issues and information and exercise sound judgment in handling sensitive or potentially sensitive topics. \u2022 Support Washburn\u2019s mission. \u2022 Perform additional job-related duties as assigned or as appropriate. Required Qualifications: \u2022 JD from an ABA-accredited law school. \u2022 Admission to the Kansas State Bar. \u2022 Experience reviewing, drafting, or negotiating contracts for a legal practice. \u2022 Demonstrated ability to synthesize complex information into easily digestible formats and combine legal considerations with program and policy objectives to develop practical solutions that meet client needs. \u2022 Demonstrated ability to thrive in a customer-service focused environment, with a collaborative working style. \u2022 Proven ability to effectively communicate legal language and analysis to non-lawyers, including when conveying unpleasant or unwelcome information. \u2022 Demonstrated ability to handle work duties and client interactions in an open, respectful manner that builds confidence and approachability in the General Counsel\u2019s office. \u2022 Proven ability to work independently, manage several projects simultaneously, and meet deadlines. \u2022 A proven work history with a commitment to the highest ethical standards. \u2022 Demonstrated ability to use sound independent judgment and professional integrity. \u2022 Proven record of providing prompt and effective research, analytical, and writing skills. \u2022 Proven ability to build and maintain professional collaborative relationships with individuals and groups across an organization, as well as stakeholders and community members. \u2022 Proven ability to prioritize and respond to issues and requests accurately and effectively. \u2022 License to practice law in Kansas. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Knowledge of FERPA, Title IX, and other regulatory frameworks applicable to colleges and universities. \u2022 Experience working in a higher education, governmental, healthcare, or other highly regulated environments. \u2022 Experience conducting compliance risk assessments, compliance reviews, audits, investigations, or corrective action planning. Exempt, Full-time, Mon-Fri, 9am-5:30pm Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) 6231bb75 Last Name (required) 9c7d1590 Email (required) a95758df Job Alert bc58d49b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments President President Categories General Counsel/Legal Staff General Counsel/Legal Staff Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Washburn University\u2019s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 73ffe6d1 Last Name (required) f7eac298 Email (required) e364b82c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking \u201cI Accept\u201d or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"}, "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-clinical-counseling-or-school-psychology-topeka-kansas-united-states-c980dded-2481-4dcc-9b22-59e17974d52f": {"title": "Assistant Professor (Clinical, Counseling, or School Psychology)", "description": "Assistant Professor (Clinical, Counseling, or School Psychology) - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Assistant Professor (Clinical, Counseling, or School Psychology) College of Arts & Sciences Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant Professor (Clinical, Counseling, or School Psychology) College of Arts & Sciences Faculty Tenure Track Position Title: Assistant Professor (Clinical, Counseling, or School Psychology) Department: Psychology Campus Location: Washburn University Position Summary: Washburn University's Department of Psychology invites applications for an assistant professor position to begin January or August 2027. This is a full-time 9-month, tenure track position. A completed doctorate is necessary for tenure-track appointment. Each selected candidate will have a demonstrated commitment to pursuing teaching excellence at Washburn University, including a dedication to developing inclusive teaching practices that engage all learners. The Psychology department is a collegial and collaborative one and consists of faculty from various areas in psychology. All faculty teach and advise our undergraduate and graduate students. Clinical faculty also supervise therapist trainees in the department\u2019s Psychological Services Clinic. Washburn provides support for faculty, undergraduate, and graduate students to present collaborative research at regional and/or national conferences each year. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: \u2022 Fulfill teaching expectations associated with tenure-track appointment. Teach 12-hours per semester (in-person and online, according to departmental needs) or equivalent full workload as outlined in the faculty handbook. \u2022 Teach and develop undergraduate and graduate classes and seminars as assigned and as dependent upon department needs, which may include Adult or Child Assessment, Adult or Child Assessment Practicum, Adult or Child Treatment, Adult or Child Treatment Practicum, Introductory Psychology, Developmental Psychology, Abnormal Psychology, Personality, Ethics as assigned by the Department Chairperson. \u2022 Supervise undergraduate and master\u2019s student research. \u2022 Have an active research program that can involve students. \u2022 Advise students and engage in service activities in the department and to the university, the profession, and/or the community. \u2022 Become licensed as a psychologist in Kansas before tenure and maintain licensure thereafter. \u2022 Perform additional job-related duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: \u2022 Ph.D. or PsyD in Clinical, Counseling, or School Psychology; ABD applicants will be considered, with completion of the Ph.D. by August 1, 2028. \u2022 Licensed or license-eligible in Kansas as a psychologist. \u2022 Graduate training or experience is appropriate to teach clinical or counseling psychology courses at the graduate/undergraduate level. \u2022 Demonstrated dedication to developing inclusive teaching practices that engage all learners. \u2022 Official educational transcripts required at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Ph.D. or PsyD in Clinical Psychology from APA accredited program. \u2022 Experience mentoring student research. \u2022 A research program relevant to clinical psychology. \u2022 Experience doing clinical supervision. \u2022 Graduate training or experience appropriate to teach Adult or Child Assessment or Adult or Child Therapy at the graduate level. Special Instructions to Applicants: \u2022 Please upload the following items as a pdf to the \u201cadditional document\u201d field via the electronic application: a cover letter (discuss how you will achieve licensure as a psychologist in Kansas), curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy highlighting inclusive teaching strategies, evidence of teaching effectiveness (such as student or peer evaluations), a statement of research and mentorship philosophy. Contact information for three current professional references will be collected as part of the application form. \u2022 If you have graduate training or experience appropriate to teach Adult or Child Assessment or Adult or Child Therapy at the graduate level please specify in your cover letter. \u2022 If you have questions about the position, please contact Dr. Julie Boydston, search committee chair, Julie.boydston@washburn.edu . Application Deadline:\u00a0\u00a0Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants can be assured of full consideration if submitted by October 19, 2026. Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) 27fad513 Last Name (required) a8b1920f Email (required) 44286d65 Job Alert 2a7acf16 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments College of Arts & Sciences College of Arts & Sciences Categories Psychology, Sociology, Anthropology, Philosophy Psychology, Sociology, Anthropology, Philosophy Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Washburn University\u2019s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 9c5f724d Last Name (required) 588b7f21 Email (required) f895ab38 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking \u201cI Accept\u201d or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"}, "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-molecular-biology-topeka-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor (Molecular Biology)", "description": "Assistant Professor (Molecular Biology) - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Assistant Professor (Molecular Biology) College of Arts & Sciences Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant Professor (Molecular Biology) College of Arts & Sciences Faculty Tenure Track Position Title: Assistant Professor (Molecular Biology) Department: Biology Campus Location: Washburn University Position Summary: Washburn University's Department of Biology invites applications for a tenure-track position as assistant professor of Biology, with a specialization in molecular biology, to begin August 1, 2027. This is a full-time, nine-month position. The selected candidate will have a demonstrated commitment to pursuing teaching excellence at Washburn University, including a dedication to developing inclusive teaching practices that engage all learners. The Washburn Biology Department offers degrees in the following majors: general biology, environmental biology, forensic biology, molecular biology & biotechnology, and biology secondary education. In addition, the department teaches several service courses that support programs in Nursing, Kinesiology, and Allied Health, among others. The successful candidate will be expected to collaborate pedagogically with a cohesive team of student-centered faculty. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: \u2022 Fulfill teaching expectations associated with tenure-track appointment. Teach 12-faculty load hours per semester (either in-person or online, according to departmental needs) or equivalent full workload as outlined in the faculty handbook. \u2022 Teach and develop undergraduate classes as assigned and as dependent upon department needs, which may include introductory human biology lecture and lab, moleculary genetics, molecular biology lecture and lab, and general cellular biology, in addition to other courses consistent with the candidate\u2019s training and interests. \u2022 Fulfill scholarship expectations associated with a tenure-track appointment. \u2022 Fulfill service expectations associated with tenure-track appointment by engaging in service activities in the department, university, and/or profession. \u2022 Establish a research program involving undergraduates. \u2022 Mentor and advise students interested in pursuing a variety of careers. \u2022 Perform additional job-related duties as assigned or as appropriate. Required Qualifications: \u2022 Doctoral degree in Molecular Biology, Biology, or closely related field. ABD applicants will be considered, with completion of the doctorate by August 1, 2028. \u2022 Demonstrated dedication to developing inclusive teaching practices that engage all learners. \u2022 Experience or potential for research in molecular biology or related discipline. \u2022 Official educational transcripts required at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Experience teaching at the university level. \u2022 Teaching experience and course development in the areas of genetics, molecular biology, and cellular biology. \u2022 Experience or potential for service at the departmental, university, and/or professional level \u2022 Experience or potential to involve undergraduate students in research projects. Special Instructions to Applicants: \u2022 Please upload the following items as .pdf files to the \u201cadditional documents\u201d field via the electronic application: a letter of interest, statement of teaching philosophy with inclusive teaching practices, evidence of teaching effectiveness (such as student or peer evaluations), and an outline of research plans \u2013 especially those involving undergraduates. Contact information for three current professional references should be entered into specific fields of the online application. \u2022 If you have questions about the position, please contact Dr. Joan Klages, Chair, Molecular Biology Search Committee joan.klages@washburn.edu . Application Deadline:\u00a0\u00a0Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants can be assured of full consideration if submitted by November 13, 2026. Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) ec0f1e95 Last Name (required) ccb8deed Email (required) fb43ef32 Job Alert 91dd4a86 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments College of Arts & Sciences College of Arts & Sciences Categories Biology/Chemistry/Physics/Astronomy Biology/Chemistry/Physics/Astronomy Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Washburn University\u2019s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 78f2da23 Last Name (required) 8c150387 Email (required) e80bce6f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking \u201cI Accept\u201d or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"}, "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/associate-professor-legal-analysis-research-and-writing-topeka-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Associate Professor (Legal Analysis, Research, and Writing)", "description": "Associate Professor (Legal Analysis, Research, and Writing) - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Associate Professor (Legal Analysis, Research, and Writing) School of Law Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Associate Professor (Legal Analysis, Research, and Writing) School of Law Faculty Tenure Track Position Title: Associate Professor (Legal Analysis, Research, and Writing) Department: School of Law Campus Location: Washburn University Position Summary: Washburn University School of Law invites applicants for a tenured/tenure-track position to teach first year Legal Analysis, Research and Writing, beginning in the 2027-2028 academic year. Washburn Law\u2019s nationally ranked legal writing program follows the typical structure for legal writing courses: objective or predictive writing in the first semester and persuasive writing and advocacy in the second semester. Both courses are three credit hours. Washburn Law has a unitary tenure track with scholarship support including summer writing grants, year-round research assistants, and funding for travel to conferences. This nine-month tenured/tenure-track position is one of three open tenured/tenure-track positions in the School of Law. We seek engaging candidates whose performance to date has demonstrated effectiveness in teaching, scholarship, and service or the potential for achievement in each of these job functions. Each selected candidate will have a demonstrated commitment to pursuing teaching excellence, including a dedication to developing inclusive teaching practices that engage all learners. The School of Law moved into its new, state-of-the-art building in July 2023. The building features classrooms equipped with up-to-date recording technology, including closed captioning; a green room recording studio; and beautiful trial and appellate courtrooms. The Washburn campus is located blocks from the historic state capitol. Topeka features affordable housing; beautiful, historic neighborhoods with well-maintained parks; and a nationally recognized public library. It is also the home of the Brown v. Board of Education National Historical Site. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: \u2022 The appointed hire will be responsible for fulfilling teaching expectations associated with a tenured/tenure-track professor appointment. \u2022 The appointed hire will be responsible for fulfilling scholarship expectations associated with a tenured/tenure-track professor appointment. \u2022 The appointed hire will be responsible for fulfilling service expectations associated with a tenured/tenure-track professor appointment. \u2022 Perform additional job-related duties as assigned or as appropriate. Required Qualifications: \u2022 JD degree from an ABA-approved law school or international equivalent. \u2022 Demonstrated interest in teaching legal research and writing. \u2022 Demonstrated dedication to developing inclusive teaching practices that engage all learners. \u2022 Demonstrated commitment to institutional service, whether university or practice related. \u2022 Demonstrated potential for scholarship. \u2022 Official educational transcripts required at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Special Instructions to Applicants: \u2022 Interested candidates should submit their resume, cover letter, and the names/addresses/phone numbers of three professional references through the Washburn University job portal at https://www.washburn.edu/faculty-staff/human-resources/employment-opportunities/index.html. \u2022 If you have questions about the position, please contact Professor Michelle Ewert, Chair, Faculty Recruitment Committee, at michelle.ewert@washburn.edu . Application Deadline:\u00a0\u00a0Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants can be assured of full consideration if submitted by August 31, 2026. (All faculty appointments are contingent upon funding.) Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) 0037e3e1 Last Name (required) f2b2bbc3 Email (required) ff02c7f9 Job Alert f6d47d6f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Law School of Law Categories Law, Legal Studies, Forensics Law, Legal Studies, Forensics Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Washburn University\u2019s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 7afa5f57 Last Name (required) 17436dc0 Email (required) d1d6b37c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking \u201cI Accept\u201d or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"}, "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/associate-professor-small-business-and-nonprofit-transactional-law-clinic-topeka-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Associate Professor (Small Business and Nonprofit Transactional Law Clinic)", "description": "Associate Professor (Small Business and Nonprofit Transactional Law Clinic) - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Associate Professor (Small Business and Nonprofit Transactional Law Clinic) School of Law Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Associate Professor (Small Business and Nonprofit Transactional Law Clinic) School of Law Faculty Tenure Track Position Title: Associate Professor (Small Business and Nonprofit Transactional Law Clinic) Department: School of Law Campus Location: Washburn University Position Summary: Washburn University School of Law invites applicants for a tenured/tenure-track position to teach in the Washburn Law Clinic and to teach complementary doctrinal courses, beginning in the 2027-2028 academic year. Washburn Law has a unitary tenure track with scholarship support including summer writing grants, year-round research assistants, and funding for travel to conferences. This nine-month tenured/tenure-track position is one of three open tenured/tenure-track positions in the School of Law. We are particularly interested in applicants qualified to teach the Small Business & Nonprofit Transactional Law Clinic. We seek engaging candidates whose performance to date has demonstrated effectiveness in teaching, scholarship, and service or the potential for achievement in each of these job functions. Each selected candidate will have a demonstrated commitment to pursuing teaching excellence, including a dedication to developing inclusive teaching practices that engage all learners. Founded in 1970, Washburn University School of Law\u2019s in-house, live client clinical program has been an integral part of the law school curriculum staffed by tenured and tenure-track positions. Washburn Law Clinic practice areas include Civil Practice, Criminal Justice, Family Justice & Immigration, and Small Business & Nonprofit Transactional Law. The Small Business & Nonprofit Transactional Law section has historically represented clients in matters involving entity formation, tax exempt status, intellectual property, and governing documents and has been actively involved in conducting community education events and other community projects. The School of Law moved into its new, state-of-the-art building in July 2023. The building features classrooms equipped with up-to-date recording technology, including closed captioning; a green room recording studio; and beautiful trial and appellate courtrooms. The Washburn campus is located blocks from the historic state capitol. Topeka features affordable housing; beautiful, historic neighborhoods with well-maintained parks; and a nationally recognized public library. It is also the home of the Brown v. Board of Education National Historical Site. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: \u2022 The appointed hire will be responsible for fulfilling teaching expectations associated with a tenured/tenure-track professor appointment. They will teach part-time in the clinic and part-time in other courses as assigned. \u2022 The appointed hire will be responsible for fulfilling scholarship expectations associated with a tenured/tenure-track professor appointment. \u2022 The appointed hire will be responsible for fulfilling service expectations associated with a tenured/tenure-track professor appointment. \u2022 Perform additional job-related duties as assigned or as appropriate. Required Qualifications: \u2022 JD degree from an ABA-approved law school. \u2022 Demonstrated commitment to clinical legal education. \u2022 Kansas bar license or eligibility to apply for a restricted license to practice in a clinical setting for the length of the appointment, which does not require the taking of the Kansas state bar exam. \u2022 Demonstrated dedication to developing inclusive teaching practices that engage all learners. \u2022 Demonstrated commitment to institutional service, whether university or practice related. \u2022 Demonstrated potential for scholarship. \u2022 Training or experience appropriate to teach in a small business and nonprofit transactional law clinic. \u2022 Official educational transcripts required at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Training or experience appropriate to teach doctrinal courses complementary to the clinic such as real estate transactions, transactional drafting, and other courses in the business curriculum Special Instructions to Applicants: \u2022 Interested candidates should submit their resume, cover letter, and the names/addresses/phone numbers of three professional references through the Washburn University job portal at https://www.washburn.edu/faculty-staff/human-resources/employment-opportunities/index.html. \u2022 If you have questions about the position, please contact Professor Michelle Ewert, Chair, Faculty Recruitment Committee, at michelle.ewert@washburn.edu. Application Deadline:\u00a0\u00a0Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants can be assured of full consideration if submitted by August 31, 2026. (All faculty appointments are contingent upon funding.) Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) fec71e3b Last Name (required) c11504b8 Email (required) 6a6e0af4 Job Alert 01f8638b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Law School of Law Categories Law, Legal Studies, Forensics Law, Legal Studies, Forensics Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Invo