captioning; a green room recording studio; and beautiful trial and appellate courtrooms. The Washburn campus is located blocks from the historic state capitol. Topeka features affordable housing; beautiful, historic neighborhoods with well-maintained parks; and a nationally recognized public library. It is also the home of the Brown v. Board of Education National Historical Site. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: \u2022 The appointed hire will be responsible for fulfilling teaching expectations associated with a tenured/tenure-track professor appointment. \u2022 The appointed hire will be responsible for fulfilling scholarship expectations associated with a tenured/tenure-track professor appointment. \u2022 The appointed hire will be responsible for fulfilling service expectations associated with a tenured/tenure-track professor appointment. \u2022 Perform additional job-related duties as assigned or as appropriate. Required Qualifications: \u2022 JD degree from an ABA-approved law school or international equivalent. \u2022 Demonstrated dedication to developing inclusive teaching practices that engage all learners. \u2022 Demonstrated commitment to institutional service, whether university or practice related. \u2022 Demonstrated potential for scholarship. \u2022 Demonstrated dedication to developing inclusive teaching practices that engage all learners. \u2022 Official educational transcripts required at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Record of practice, teaching, and/or scholarship in the areas of constitutional law, administrative law, legislation, property, evidence, professional responsibility, or remedies. Special Instructions to Applicants: \u2022 Interested candidates should submit their resume, cover letter, and the names/addresses/phone numbers of three professional references through the Washburn University job portal at https://www.washburn.edu/faculty-staff/human-resources/employment-opportunities/index.html. \u2022 If you have questions about the position, please contact Professor Michelle Ewert, Chair, Faculty Recruitment Committee, at michelle.ewert@washburn.edu . Application Deadline:\u00a0\u00a0Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants can be assured of full consideration if submitted by August 31, 2026. (All faculty appointments are contingent upon funding.) Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) 4e9809fa Last Name (required) 43bd0240 Email (required) 7f3e9d3e Job Alert 86734cbb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Law School of Law Categories Law, Legal Studies, Forensics Law, Legal Studies, Forensics Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Washburn University\u2019s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) f2c52e89 Last Name (required) c08ae264 Email (required) d641bd26 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking \u201cI Accept\u201d or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"}, "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/broadcasting-engineer-topeka-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Broadcasting Engineer", "description": "Broadcasting Engineer - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Broadcasting Engineer KTWU Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Broadcasting Engineer KTWU Staff Full-time Position Title: Broadcasting Engineer Department: KTWU - General Advertised Pay: Base $20.39/hour with potential for a higher entry rate commensurate with experience Campus Location: Washburn University Application Review: Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Position Summary: This position is a crucial component to the monitoring and maintaining of KTWU\u2019s high-quality broadcast signal to viewers in Eastern Kansas. This position reports to the Assistant Chief Engineer and serves as master control operator, ensuring seamless delivery of KTWU broadcast channels via OTA, cable, fiber, and streaming; monitors satellite, file download, and cloud-based delivery of content; ensures content is available for air on KTWU\u2019s video server and archive system; ensures KTWU broadcast signal is compliant with FCC policies and procedures (weather/emergency alerts, closed-captioning, audio levels, etc.); and assists with maintenance projects and equipment installation as needed in master control, production control, studio, transmitter, and SE Kansas translator. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: \u2022 Serves as Master Control operator. Monitors KTWU\u2019s OTA (over the air), cable, fiber, and streaming signals for all content delivery platforms that carry KTWU channels; ensures content is downloaded and checked prior to broadcast; and monitors KTWU\u2019s automation system, online video server, and archive system. Ensures weather/emergency alerts and closed-captioning are broadcast according to FCC policies and procedures. Monitors closed-captioning, audio and video levels of programs, making needed adjustments to maintain KTWU\u2019s OTA standards. \u2022 Works with KTWU\u2019s Traffic Department to implement and maintain the broadcast log, ensuring all scheduled content is in the video server for playout and identifying differences, errors, and any changes that occur after broadcast log is submitted to Traffic to ensure an accurate as-run log. \u2022 Observes operations and monitors transmitters to ensure equipment is operating at maximum e\ufb03ciency and in accordance with FCC rules and regulations. Noti\ufb01es Chief Engineer or Assistant Chief Engineer if problems develop to seek direction and make or facilitate correction. \u2022 Repairs and checks various pieces of equipment used in the origination and transmission of programs to identify and resolve problems or report them to the Assistant Chief Engineer if needed. Performs routine maintenance to assist engineering sta\ufb00 as directed. \u2022 Works with KTWU\u2019s Traffic Department to ensure on-air promos are tagged and ready for broadcast in the video server. \u2022 Supports other KTWU departments and team members during community and fundraising events to assist with continued sustainability of KTWU\u2019s services and mission to Kansas communities. \u2022 Performs other job-related duties as assigned or as appropriate. Required Qualifications: \u2022 High school, GED, or equivalent. \u2022 Basic knowledge of computers and electronic test equipment. \u2022 Must be able to work unsupervised. \u2022 Critical thinking skills. \u2022 Must be able to work non-standard hours, weekends, and holidays. Physical Requirements: \u2022 Ability to move and/or maneuver equipment weighing approximately 50 pounds. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Work experience as a Master Control Operator or completion of technical school program in electronics. \u2022 An aptitude for working with technical equipment at a television station. \u2022 Knowledge of digital equipment. \u2022 Certification by the Society of Broadcast Engineers. Hourly, Full-time, Varies, Varies/Shift Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) fe53995d Last Name (required) fe67a50d Email (required) 223588a9 Job Alert 596523ee Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments KTWU KTWU Categories Arts, Museum Admin, Television Arts, Museum Admin, Television Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Washburn University\u2019s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 295cafd0 Last Name (required) f3d759db Email (required) 82514f56 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking \u201cI Accept\u201d or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"}, "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/campus-safety-dispatcher-part-time-temporary-two-positions-topeka-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Campus Safety Dispatcher (Part-time, Temporary) (Two Positions)", "description": "Campus Safety Dispatcher (Part-time, Temporary) (Two Positions) - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Campus Safety Dispatcher (Part-time, Temporary) (Two Positions) University Police Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Campus Safety Dispatcher (Part-time, Temporary) (Two Positions) University Police Staff Temporary Position Title: Campus Safety Dispatcher (Part-time, Temporary) (Two Positions) Department: University Police Advertised Pay: $20.39/hr Campus Location: Washburn University Application Review: Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Position Summary: The Campus Safety Dispatcher for the Washburn Police Department receives telephone calls for assistance and emergency police services from persons on the Washburn University Campus, and monitors alarm systems in campus buildings, the environmental computer, and Emergency Help Phones on campus. Determines appropriate response(s) based on the scope and urgency of reported and observed incidents and summons officer(s) to assist. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: \u2022 Regular and reliable attendance is critical due to operational needs to ensure public safety and prompt emergency service to the community. \u2022 Receives and transmits information to and requests from officers in the field via police radio. Retrieves requested information by operating the NCIC computer and KCJIS computer to perform record checks, warrant checks, driver\u2019s license checks, and vehicle registration checks. Keeps a constant accounting of the location, status, and safety of all officers. Types call information into the CAD computer to establish a record of the daily activities during the shift. \u2022 Interfaces with the campus community to assist with lost and found items and give information and directions about the campus when requested. Maintains the key check-out log and the visitor log. \u2022 Monitors the Closed Circuit Television Cameras and the campus surveillance cameras for suspicious activities and reports such activities to the officers in the field. \u2022 Performs additional job-related duties as assigned or appropriate. Required Qualifications: \u2022 High school diploma, GED, or equivalent. \u2022 Ability to monitor multiple devices, complete required forms using appropriate software, follow department procedures, and carry out assigned tasks almost simultaneously. \u2022 Familiarity with personal computers and Windows-based applications. Physical Requirements: \u2022 Must be a US Citizen, US National, Permanent Resident Alien of the US, or Non-Citizen with unrestricted employment authorization and be at least 18 years of age. \u2022 A criminal background check that includes a drug screening is required once a contingent offer is made. \u2022 Will also be required to pass a hearing and vision test. \u2022 Ability to sit in a chair for long periods. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Experience working in a law enforcement agency and a communication center. \u2022 One year of customer service experience providing information, responding to inquiries, or explaining policies, rules, and regulations in person or by telephone. Special Instructions to Applicants: Hourly, Part-time, Temporary Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) 1d693bce Last Name (required) 5d9d6b37 Email (required) a16c9cf6 Job Alert 175cb923 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments University Police University Police Categories Police and Public Safety Police and Public Safety Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Washburn University\u2019s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) e994ce00 Last Name (required) a63eacaa Email (required) b71b6dde Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking \u201cI Accept\u201d or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"}, "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/carpenter-topeka-kansas-united-states-99578e79-9462-4a6f-b24a-5efa0e516f71": {"title": "Carpenter", "description": "Carpenter - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Carpenter Facilities Services Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Carpenter Facilities Services Staff Full-time Position Title: Carpenter Department: Facilities Services (CBU) Advertised Pay: $21.63/hour Campus Location: Washburn University Application Review: Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Position Summary: This position performs the duties of a Carpenter. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: \u2022 Employees are expected to use equipment to manufacturer and University standards and to comply with University and OSHA policies and regulations. \u2022 New employees must complete safety training within 6 months of hire. \u2022 As assigned or requested via work orders, construct, repair and maintain structures such as furniture, partitions, walls, platforms, paneling, siding, window frames, stairways, doors and door frames and other structures using hand and power tools and performing a variety of construction duties, including but not limited to carpentry, plastering, ceiling tile and grid repairs; roof repairs such as wooden trim, soffit or shingle roof tiles; floor repair such as install small quantity of floor tiles or patch floor tiles; and masonry and minor demolition. \u2022 Review building plans, blueprints, sketches, etc., estimate and requisition type and quantity of materials required to complete projects. \u2022 Work with other facilities and University staff, offices, etc. to coordinate activities to accomplish carpentry work. \u2022 Install and maintain doors. \u2022 Maintain and repair locks on doors, windows, and furniture. \u2022 Record and document completed tasks using Computerized Maintenance Management System software. \u2022 Inspect completed work for quality standards, code, and regulation compliance. \u2022 Recommend work process improvements to Facilities supervisors and administrators. \u2022 Assist with general maintenance activities as assigned. \u2022 Provide service support for campus events. \u2022 Maintain a professional, safe, and clean work area. \u2022 Snow removal duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: \u2022 High school diploma, GED, or equivalent. \u2022 A combination of five (5) years of experience working as a Carpenter acquired through on-the-job training and/or a completed certification program. \u2022 Ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing. \u2022 Ability to read and apply information from schematics and building blueprints. \u2022 Valid driver's license with an acceptable driving record under Washburn's standards. Physical Requirements: \u2022 This position is designated a safety sensitive position and will be required to undergo drug screening. \u2022 Ability to work from a ladder and/or a lift. \u2022 Ability to respond to emergency service calls outside regularly scheduled work hours. \u2022 Ability to move and/or maneuver equipment and materials weighing as much as 50 pounds. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Skills as a locksmith. \u2022 Experience with a Computerized Maintenance Management System. Hourly, Full-time, Mon-Fri, 8am-4:30pm Background check, driving history, and drug screen are required. Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) 4cd7468f Last Name (required) 74953d72 Email (required) d68f4aae Job Alert 51cdd056 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Facilities Services Facilities Services Categories Facilities Maint/HVAC/Mgmt. Facilities Maint/HVAC/Mgmt. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Washburn University\u2019s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) ba867cb2 Last Name (required) 1d800940 Email (required) 230ca7ff Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking \u201cI Accept\u201d or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"}, "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/construction-project-coordinator-topeka-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Construction Project Coordinator", "description": "Construction Project Coordinator - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Construction Project Coordinator Facilities Services Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Construction Project Coordinator Facilities Services Staff Full-time Position Title: Construction Project Coordinator Department: Facilities Services Advertised Pay: Lower $70,000's Campus Location: Washburn University ApplicationReview: Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Position Summary: Primary responsibilities are to assist with the organization of the operations of construction on Washburn campuses by assisting with the coordination of resources and equipment for construction projects, with the goal of getting them completed accurately, on time, and within budget. Projects may range from new construction or renovations to program specific equipment installations. This position may be asked to help with concept development, design, planning, bidding, and/or implementation processes. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: \u2022 Support staff with project management throughout the construction process for new construction, major renovations, and/or alterations to campus facilities to ensure the University's expectations and requirements are met. \u2022 Work with architectural and engineering firms along with staff and other University stakeholders during all phases of construction to verify the project is reflective of the design/construction plans. \u2022 May serve as a liaison among campus departments and external contractors for coordinating and scheduling projects. \u2022 Assist with monitoring construction sites to ensure projects have necessary resources, are completed on time, and within budget. \u2022 Inspect projects, drawings, and documents to ensure compliance with specifications and standards. \u2022 Assist with the studies and observations of the physical needs of Washburn campuses and coordinate the necessary repairs, renovations, and/or alterations to Washburn facilities. \u2022 Support staff in management of project timelines to report and adjust for delays and emergencies as they arise. \u2022 Facilitate acquisition of needed materials, tools, and equipment. \u2022 Ensure appropriate permits are obtained and filed. \u2022 Assist with monitoring project costs. \u2022 Work with contractors to address issues that arise during construction. With assistance from staff, identify acceptable approaches to resolve issues within time and cost constraints. \u2022 Continually update project files (as-built drawings, test reports, O&M manuals, cost data, insurance documents and warranties) for reporting and project management. \u2022 Assist with maintenance of university records (project records, shop drawings, original equipment manufacturer manuals, etc.) using department software. Collaborate with staff to complete paperwork (budgets, cost estimates, upkeep, etc.), including project closeout process. \u2022 Provide assistance with project research and resolution. \u2022 Support staff in the preparation of reports, collecting and formulating data. Work collaboratively to assist with the preparation of the budget for yearly capital improvement requests. \u2022 Assist staff with updating floor plans and campus and utility maps. \u2022 May attend meetings to provide assistance to other units within the department, or to represent the department throughout campus. \u2022 Perform additional job-related duties as assigned or as appropriate. Non-Essential Functions: \u2022 Coordinates furniture selection for departments. Required Qualifications: \u2022 Bachelor\u2019s degree in engineering, architecture, architectural engineering, or construction management. \u2022 Previous construction experience required. \u2022 Demonstrated effective interpersonal skills. \u2022 Valid driver\u2019s license with a driving record that meets Washburn standards. Physical Requirements: \u2022 Ability to work from a ladder or lift, tour the campus, buildings, and job sites, which may include uneven surfaces and/or stairs. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Two years of construction project management experience. \u2022 Knowledge in Revit or Auto CAD. \u2022 Experience with ADA, building, and life safety codes. \u2022 Proficient MS Office Suite skills. \u2022 Proven ability to handle multiple projects with evidence of completion within established budget and timelines. Exempt, Full-time Background check and driving history are required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) 75f28f41 Last Name (required) 51b3f441 Email (required) 06393d78 Job Alert ac296d7a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Facilities Services Facilities Services Categories Facilities Maint/HVAC/Mgmt. Facilities Maint/HVAC/Mgmt. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Washburn University\u2019s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 8955f7c0 Last Name (required) f4ecd927 Email (required) e5192c90 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking \u201cI Accept\u201d or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"}, "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/construction-project-manager-topeka-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Construction Project Manager (Updated 8/24/2026)", "description": "Construction Project Manager (Updated 8/24/2026) - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Construction Project Manager (Updated 8/24/2026) Facilities Services Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Construction Project Manager (Updated 8/24/2026) Facilities Services Staff Full-time Position Title: Construction Project Manager (Updated 8/24/2026) Department: Facilities Services Advertised Pay: Upper $80,000\u2019s to Mid $90,000\u2019s Campus Location: Washburn University Application Deadline: Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Position Summary: The Construction Project Manager will provide professional project management of design and construction projects for university facilities. Projects may include new construction, fit-out of shell spaces, renovation of existing spaces, and maintenance of existing buildings and campus infrastructure. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: \u2022 Demonstrate leadership, management, organization, and communication skills. Provide excellent customer service to meet client needs and university standards. \u2022 Provide professional direction for project teams to achieve common goals and successful projects. \u2022 Provide consistent, timely, and reliable communication between all project stakeholders, including clients, professional service providers, university personnel, and contractors, to ensure that projects are thoroughly documented and understood. \u2022 Lead the development of project scope, budget, and schedule for multiple projects or tasks simultaneously. \u2022 Manage and track project budgets and schedules to ensure timely completion of projects within the established budgets and develop reports as directed. \u2022 Maintain up-to-date project reporting. \u2022 Coordinate in-house review of contract documents with appropriate departments and staff. \u2022 Procure services of design professionals, contractors, and vendors, and administer agreements. \u2022 Review and approve requisitions and payments to contractors, architects, engineers, and vendors. \u2022 Coordinate with contractors and other personnel as necessary to manage change orders and any other issues identified during the build phase. \u2022 Administer rules and policies relating to architectural excellence and construction priorities, and recommend new and improved programs for effectively managing construction and renovation projects. \u2022 Stay abreast of legislation, building codes, building materials and methods, and university design and construction standards. \u2022 Learn and maintain awareness of project safety requirements, following OSHA standards. \u2022 Participate in committees, task forces, etc., to improve the departmental mission of excellent customer service and project delivery. \u2022 Perform additional job-related duties as assigned or as appropriate. Required Qualifications: \u2022 Bachelor's degree in architecture, engineering, construction management, or related field. \u2022 Three or more years of progressively responsible professional experience in planning, contract administration, technical supervision, and construction and project management. \u2022 Proven ability to interpret architectural/construction drawings, specifications, codes, standards, and regulatory requirements. \u2022 Demonstrated knowledge of the principles, concepts, and methodology in designing, estimating, planning, and inspecting construction projects and managing project schedules. \u2022 Demonstrated understanding of the principles and practices of project planning, development, and evaluation. \u2022 Experience with permitting, code compliance, and local, state, and federal regulatory requirements. \u2022 Proven effective abilities to organize and execute small and large projects. \u2022 Effective technical writing skills sufficient to author contracts, specifications, reports, and general office, university, or departmental policies and procedures. \u2022 Working knowledge of complex and detailed technical contract language. \u2022 Demonstrated effective interpersonal, communication, and organizational skills. \u2022 Proven proficiency using basic office equipment, personal computer, and Microsoft Excel, Outlook, and Word software. \u2022 Demonstrated knowledge of building codes, ADA, planning, design, and construction. Physical Requirements: \u2022 Must have the ability to ascend and descend ladders and stairs. \u2022 Capable of lifting and maneuvering equipment weighing up to fifty pounds. \u2022 May be required to travel, including to remote work sites. \u2022 May be required to work on-call, weekends, and evenings. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Experience utilizing Computer aided drafting (CAD). \u2022 Licensees/Certifications/Registration. Exempt, Full-time, Mon-Fri, 8am-5pm Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) a59fa0cc Last Name (required) 877a6336 Email (required) 5a04cc00 Job Alert 9b6c3615 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Facilities Services Facilities Services Categories Architecture/Planning/Engineering Architecture/Planning/Engineering Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Washburn University\u2019s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 0220de30 Last Name (required) 53f8f1b6 Email (required) b17560fe Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking \u201cI Accept\u201d or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"}, "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/cosmetology-substitute-instructor-topeka-kansas-united-states-8635a42c-651e-4cfb-a853-d2c95a2bf5f4": {"title": "Cosmetology Substitute Instructor", "description": "Cosmetology Substitute Instructor - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Cosmetology Substitute Instructor WIT-Other Technical Programs Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Cosmetology Substitute Instructor WIT-Other Technical Programs Staff Part-Time Position Title: Cosmetology Substitute Instructor Department: WIT-Instructor Professional Development Advertised Pay: $25/hour Campus Location: Washburn Tech Application Review: Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants can be assured of full consideration if submitted by June 29, 2026. Position Summary: Cosmetology Substitute Instructors at Washburn University Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech) support classroom activity in the absence of the full-time instructor. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: \u2022 Implement lesson plans and instructions as directed by the absent instructor. \u2022 Maintain classroom discipline and adhere to the designated classroom schedule. Required Qualifications: \u2022 Two years of experience (4000 hours) working in Cosmetology or military experience equivalent to two years of experience in Cosmetology. \u2022 Active Kansas Board of Cosmetology License \u2022 Active Kansas Board of Cosmetology Instructor License. Hourly, Part-time, Temporary Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) 28017c69 Last Name (required) aa9f1ec7 Email (required) fa7c3af5 Job Alert caf92e24 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments WIT-Other Technical Programs WIT-Other Technical Programs Categories Vocational Career/Training/Advising Vocational Career/Training/Advising Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Washburn University\u2019s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) ada84ee2 Last Name (required) 203bf6f4 Email (required) 9b5c3611 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking \u201cI Accept\u201d or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"}, "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/title-ix-equal-opportunity-director-topeka-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Director of Non-Discrimination Initiatives \u2013 Title IX Administrator", "description": "Director of Non-Discrimination Initiatives \u2013 Title IX Administrator - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Director of Non-Discrimination Initiatives \u2013 Title IX Administrator President Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Director of Non-Discrimination Initiatives \u2013 Title IX Administrator President Staff Full-time Position Title: Director of Non-Discrimination Initiatives \u2013 Title IX Administrator and ADA/Section 504 Coordinator Department: Equal Opportunity Advertised Pay: Lower $100,000's Campus Location: Washburn University Application Review: Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Position Summary: This position oversees Washburn\u2019s compliance efforts with Title IX, Title VI, Title VII, the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), Section 504, NCAA membership compliance, and related Washburn policies and state and federal laws. This includes leading and/or coordinating investigations; developing, implementing, and monitoring programs and training that foster a culture of prevention and reporting around civil rights matters. The employee must maintain a high level of confidentiality and discretion in all situations and circumstances. The Director serves both Washburn University and Washburn University Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role reports to the General Counsel, with dotted lines of support to the President and Associate Vice President, Human Resources. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: \u2022 Coordinate and manage all reports of potential Title IX investigations and cases involving students, faculty, and/or staff, ensuring the process is timely, accurate, thorough, and impartial. \u2022 Conduct, oversee, and manage Title VI and Title VII investigations into allegations of discrimination, retaliation, and harassment involving students, faculty, and/or staff. Co-chair Washburn\u2019s Bias Incident Report Team. \u2022 Manage internal investigators, including recruitment, training, ongoing education, and case oversight. \u2022 Advise senior leadership on matters involving discrimination, harassment, sexual misconduct, and retaliation. \u2022 Oversee external investigators. \u2022 Ensure appropriate evidentiary collection and comprehensive investigative responses to claims of sexual violence, discrimination, and harassment. \u2022 Work with the Athletics Department to ensure compliance with NCAA guidelines, policies, and regulations. \u2022 Develop, maintain, and sustain partnerships and MOUs with community agencies, including overseeing their presence on campus. \u2022 Serve as the ADA/Section 504 (Americans with Disabilities Act) Coordinator; handle grievances relating to the accommodations process or disability discrimination/harassment. Work with the Director of Student Accessibility Services and Associate Vice President, Human Resources to ensure compliance with the ADA/Section 504 (Americans with Disabilities Act). \u2022 Design, lead, and coordinate training for students, staff, and faculty on all issues of discrimination, harassment, and sexual misconduct. \u2022 Develop and implement surveys as appropriate; work with Strategic Analysis, Research and Reporting on report writing and its proper dissemination. Utilize findings to enhance Washburn\u2019s effectiveness and compliance. \u2022 Serve as Institutional Title IX and Title VI Coordinator, ensuring compliance. Make recommendations to the appropriate division head and/or Human Resources as appropriate. \u2022 Stay up-to-date with changes to federal and state guidelines and requirements and update policies and protocols as necessary; ensure webpages are up to date. \u2022 Maintain confidential record keeping including all intake documentation for access issues and reported sexual violence, utilizing the Maxient system, climate survey results and data, and intake documentation in accordance with the law and Washburn policies. \u2022 Performs all other duties and responsibilities as assigned or directed by the supervisor. This may include attendance of and participation in required training for role or additional tasks. Required Qualifications: \u2022 Master's degree required. \u2022 Five years of experience in EEO, employment law, Title VI, Title VII, Title IX, civil rights, ADA, or other relevant experience. \u2022 Three years of experience conducting prompt, thorough, and equitable investigations regarding allegations of harassment, discrimination, sexual misconduct, sexual violence, or equivalent legal experience. \u2022 Experience designing and conducting training and professional development opportunities related to anti-harassment, non-discrimination, Title IX, or ADA in various formats. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Juris Doctor degree. \u2022 EEO experience in a higher education environment. \u2022 Knowledge of current state and federal laws and regulations, best practices, and trends in the field of education related to discrimination, harassment, and retaliation that violate Title VI, Title VII, Title IX, VAWA, and the ADA. \u2022 Effective communication and presentation skills. \u2022 Proven ability to present information clearly and concisely to individuals and groups. \u2022 Demonstrated ability to exercise independent initiative, sound judgment, maintain objectivity, and safeguard confidential and sensitive information. Exempt, Full-time Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) c235b541 Last Name (required) ab9ff675 Email (required) 1036f717 Job Alert b1ffcbce Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments President President Categories Human Resources/EEO/Title IX Human Resources/EEO/Title IX Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Washburn University\u2019s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 764db834 Last Name (required) d533847e Email (required) 06c64d7f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking \u201cI Accept\u201d or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"}, "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/director-student-affairs-topeka-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Director, Student Affairs", "description": "Director, Student Affairs - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Staff Full-time Position Title: Director, Student Affairs Department: WIT-Student Life Advertised Pay: Mid $80,000's Campus Location: Washburn Tech Application Review: Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Position Summary: This position serves as the lead student affairs professional for the Washburn University Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech) campuses and is responsible for the student life functions of student conduct and conflict resolution while facilitating campus leadership to provide Student Life operations. Responsible for working closely with the Dean of Washburn Tech, oversee student conduct and behavior communications with high school partners, and assist with providing Student Life perspectives on Washburn Tech campuses. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: \u2022 Provides leadership and supports the planning, organizing, and coordination of Student Life strategic priorities throughout Washburn Tech campuses, while achieving institutional goals and objectives and ensuring that student life services are provided to achieve educational success. \u2022 Serve as the lead student conduct officer for students at the Washburn Tech campuses. Meet with students, parents, and high school partners as appropriate to explain conduct processes. \u2022 Supervise, support, and manage assigned staff to maximize employee performance and facilitate professional growth. Recruit, hire, train, schedule, and evaluate the performance and effectiveness of assigned staff. Provide appropriate feedback and professional development opportunities. Work to maintain a healthy work environment by exercising teamwork and collaboration. As a team leader, will actively promote a professional workplace of mutual respect and collegiality for all members of the institution and work to build positive and cooperative relationships with all staff, encouraging them to work toward individual and departmental goals. \u2022 Lead communication with high school partners and Washburn Tech faculty to provide training and development (internal and external) to ensure access and awareness of Washburn Student Life programs, resources, policies, and procedures. \u2022 Will seek input from appropriate Washburn departments and staff, including student life senior leadership, to examine facts, discuss concerns, and identify available alternatives that may apply to more complex behavior cases from the Washburn Tech campuses. Determine and issue the final dispensation of each conduct case, working to the extent possible to provide direction and support to the student to help them become a better student and individual. \u2022 Participate in the University Behavioral Assessment Team (UBAT) and respond to emergencies, providing initial intervention and services to students in crisis. \u2022 Collaborate with leadership of Student Life units to facilitate the delivery of services directly to students on the Washburn Tech campuses, which may include strategic planning and/or supporting programs that are crucial to the retention of students and staff. \u2022 Provide oversight and input related to organizational realities, uphold policies and procedures, and help ensure student life operations continuously improve. \u2022 Develop an effective relationship with leadership to create a network of support for students at Washburn Tech and provide information and support to academic leadership as appropriate. \u2022 Systematically assess student life services using student learning outcomes and other appropriate measures to improve the effectiveness of these services. \u2022 Assume responsibility and leadership to complete special projects/assignments as directed. \u2022 Provide feedback to the student life senior leadership regarding activities and issues at the Washburn Tech campuses involving all Student Life Departments to facilitate onsite operational support specifically regarding how those offices are providing resources and support on Washburn Tech campuses, including, but not limited to, student accommodations and counseling services. \u2022 Represent Student Life interests on committees, task forces, and shared governance councils as appropriate. \u2022 Serve as an on-site resource for student life questions and staff and direct inquiries accordingly. \u2022 Perform additional job-related duties as assigned or as appropriate. Required Qualifications: \u2022 Master's degree. \u2022 Four years of progressively responsible experience with student conduct in a university or K-12 environment. \u2022 Supervisory experience. \u2022 Proven effective interpersonal, communication, organizational, administrative, and leadership skills. \u2022 Demonstrated ability to manage conflict and lead collaborative efforts among multiple constituencies successfully. Exempt, Full-time, Mon-Fri, 7:30am - 4:30pm Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) 08d6837d Last Name (required) be1924fa Email (required) 211628cf Job Alert d1560b42 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments WIT-Administration WIT-Administration Categories Student Life/Organizations Student Life/Organizations Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Washburn University\u2019s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. University Counselor / Campus Advocate (Two positions) Counseling Washburn University is accepting applications to hire two University Counselor / Campus Advocate positions. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 2e375dad Last Name (required) 450968d3 Email (required) eb20610a Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking \u201cI Accept\u201d or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"}, "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/graduate-assistant-athletics-external-relations-topeka-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Graduate Assistant - Athletics External Relations", "description": "Graduate Assistant - Athletics External Relations - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Graduate Assistant - Athletics External Relations Office of the Director of Athletics Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Graduate Assistant - Athletics External Relations Office of the Director of Athletics Student Position Title: Graduate Assistant - Athletics External Relations Department: Athletics Advertised Pay: Stipend + Meal Plan Provided Campus Location: Washburn University Position Summary: This position offers a unique opportunity for the selected candidate to gain hands-on experience in the intercollegiate sports industry. The individual will play a key role in enhancing the Washburn Athletics brand, expanding its fanbase, and elevating the overall gameday experience within the highly competitive Mid-America Intercollegiate Athletics Association (MIAA), the premier conference in NCAA Division II. The selected candidate will assist with all aspects of Washburn Athletics External Relations. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: -Support game day operations and marketing for all Washburn University Athletics varsity sports. -Manage and direct all marketing efforts for assigned sports to include advertising, fan experience, in-game promotions, and game scripts (while assisting with all other sports during the academic year). -Recruit, coordinate, and oversee a team of student workers or volunteers. -Responsible for growing student engagement for all sports and increasing affinity amongst students. -Contribute to video production, graphic design, social media content, and other creative initiatives for the athletics department. -Organize and oversee community engagement programs, including Bods Care and Kids Club Program. -Perform other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: -Bachelor\u2019s degree. -Job contingent on admission into the Washburn University Graduate School and the completion of a successful background check. -Must be willing to work long hours including nights, weekends, and holidays in addition to weekly office hours scheduled around university classes. -Maintain a minimum cumulative and semester GPA of 2.5. -Ability to problem solve, manage multiple tasks, adhere to deadlines, and prioritize work. Preferred Qualifications: -Experience with Daktronics, Sports Sound Pro/Sound Director, Microsoft 365, and Adobe Creative Suite products. -Innovative, creative, and energetic personality that will recommend and implement new ideas. -Ability to problem solve, manage multiple tasks, adhere to deadlines, and prioritize work. -Experience in marketing and promotions for an athletics program. -Degree in marketing, sports management, or a related field of study. Special Instructions to Applicants: Stipend Monthly Exempt, Part time, Varies, Varies/Shift Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) 7888edf7 Last Name (required) 0dba86dc Email (required) 893a978a Job Alert a58267f8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Office of the Director of Athletics Office of the Director of Athletics Categories Student Employee Student Employee Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Washburn University\u2019s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) adb79422 Last Name (required) 93c6bacc Email (required) b65a5de6 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking \u201cI Accept\u201d or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"}, "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/instructional-librarian-topeka-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Instructional Librarian", "description": "Instructional Librarian - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Instructional Librarian University Library Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Instructional Librarian University Library Faculty Lecturer Position Title: Instructional Librarian Department: University Library Campus Location: Washburn University Position Summary: Washburn University's University Libraries invites applications for Instructional Librarian to begin October 1, 2026. This is a 12-month, benefit eligible, full-time position. The Instructional Librarian provides general and virtual information, research, and reference services, plans, teaches and assesses information literacy instruction in collaboration with the Associate Dean of University Libraries and other appropriate staff. In addition, based upon disciplinary interest, expertise, and Unit needs, the Librarian will support other library initiatives, including but not limited to: faculty and student research, digital projects, First and Second-Year Student Success Initiatives, collection development, scholarly communication, Open Access and Open Educational Resources, Artificial Intelligence, outreach and assessment. Each selected candidate will have a demonstrated commitment to pursuing teaching excellence at Washburn University, including a dedication to developing inclusive teaching practices that engage all learners. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: \u2022 Serve as liaison to academic departments. Locate and create digital content to support academic instruction. \u2022 Teach, integrate and assess Information Literacy programs across the curriculum. \u2022 Provide expert information and research services. \u2022 Explore, evaluate, and encourage the deployment of emergent technologies into library programs, information and instructional services. \u2022 Develop outreach strategies for students and faculty. \u2022 Participate in the building of physical and electronic collections that meet the needs of Washburn University. \u2022 Develop web and print-based materials. \u2022 Librarians are active members of internal library teams, Library and University Committees. \u2022 Perform additional job-related duties as assigned or as appropriate. Required Qualifications: \u2022 ALA-accredited master\u2019s degree at the time of application or by the end of the semester of hire. \u2022 Experience providing reference or instruction services in archives, special collections, research libraries, museums, or cultural institutions. \u2022 Demonstrated understanding of issues and trends in reference and information literacy. \u2022 Proven effective interpersonal and communication skills. \u2022 Proven ability to work effectively independently and in teams. \u2022 Demonstrated experience providing accurate, proactive, and responsive information services. \u2022 Demonstrated dedication to developing inclusive teaching practices that engage all learners. \u2022 Official educational transcripts required at the time of hire. Physical Requirements: \u2022 Occasionally lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects weighing less than 20 pounds Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 An additional master\u2019s degree in any subject taught at Washburn University. \u2022 Demonstrated ability to work effectively independently or as part of a team. \u2022 Two years of experience providing reference or instruction services in archives, special collections or a research library, museum, or cultural institution. \u2022 Experience in a higher education library. Special Instructions to Applicants: Inquiries regarding this position may be directed to the Screening Committee Chair, Sean Stacey at sean.stacey@washburn.edu . Application Deadline: Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants can be assured of full consideration if submitted by September 15, 2026. Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) 4e7b314f Last Name (required) 3ac8d504 Email (required) 5f20aa59 Job Alert c92f6adf Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments University Library University Library Categories Librarians Librarians Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts.