es, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"}, "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/lecturer-sociology-topeka-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Lecturer (Sociology)", "description": "Lecturer (Sociology) - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Lecturer (Sociology) College of Arts & Sciences Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Lecturer (Sociology) College of Arts & Sciences Faculty Lecturer Position Title: Lecturer (Sociology) Department: Sociology & Anthropology Campus Location: Washburn University Position Summary: Washburn University's Department of Sociology and Anthropology invites applications for a Sociology Lecturer to begin in August 2027. This is a full-time, nine-month, non-tenure-track position with a renewable annual contract. Each selected candidate will have a demonstrated commitment to pursuing teaching excellence at Washburn University, including a dedication to developing inclusive teaching practices that engage all learners. The Sociology program offers students the opportunity to participate in community-engaged learning, conduct research independently, and study abroad. Classes and advising cohorts are small, allowing for meaningful faculty-student collaboration. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: \u2022 Fulfill teaching expectations associated with non-tenure-track appointment. Teach 12 credit hours per semester (either in-person or online, according to departmental needs) or equivalent full-time workload as outlined in the faculty handbook. \u2022 Teach and develop undergraduate classes and seminars as assigned, dependent upon department needs, which may include Criminology, Deviance, Social Problems, or some combination of classes consistent with the candidate\u2019s training and interests. \u2022 Advise students and engage in service expectations associated with a non-tenure-track appointment. \u2022 Perform additional job-related duties as assigned or as appropriate. Required Qualifications: \u2022 Ph.D. in Sociology; ABD applicants will be considered, with completion of the doctorate by August 2028. \u2022 Experience teaching undergraduate sociology course(s). \u2022 Evidence of excellence in teaching at the university level. \u2022 Demonstrated dedication to developing inclusive teaching practices that engage all learners. \u2022 Official educational transcripts required at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Experience as the sole instructor for undergraduate sociology course(s). \u2022 Experience teaching courses in Social Problems. \u2022 Experience teaching courses in Criminology, Deviance, and/or Law and Society. \u2022 Documented department and/or university service. Special Instructions to Applicants: \u2022 Please upload the following items as a .pdf file to the \u201cadditional document\u201d field in the electronic application: A cover letter including a statement of teaching philosophy and evidence of teaching excellence. Contact information for three professional references will be collected as part of the application. \u2022 If you have questions about the position, please contact Dr. Lindsey Iba\u00f1ez, Search Committee Chair, at lindsey.ibanez@washburn.edu . \u2022 The successful candidate will be required to provide official transcripts and to submit to a background check prior to hire. Application Deadline:\u00a0\u00a0Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants can be assured of full consideration if submitted by October 1, 2026. Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) df766f1f Last Name (required) 22e9bdbf Email (required) 89797cfc Job Alert 0f6f7e11 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments College of Arts & Sciences College of Arts & Sciences Categories Psychology, Sociology, Anthropology, Philosophy Psychology, Sociology, Anthropology, Philosophy Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Washburn University\u2019s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 0a1c71ab Last Name (required) c8f3484a Email (required) c05e5152 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking \u201cI Accept\u201d or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"}, "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/lecturer-or-assistant-professor-biology-anatomy-topeka-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Lecturer or Assistant Professor (Biology Anatomy)", "description": "Lecturer or Assistant Professor (Biology Anatomy) - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Lecturer or Assistant Professor (Biology Anatomy) College of Arts & Sciences Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Lecturer or Assistant Professor (Biology Anatomy) College of Arts & Sciences Faculty Lecturer Position Title: Lecturer or Assistant Professor (Biology Anatomy) Department: Biology Campus Location: Washburn University Position Summary: Washburn University's Department of Biology invites applications for an open position in Biology, with a specialization in anatomy, at either the lecturer or assistant professor rank. A candidate hired into a non-tenure-track appointment may be eligible for conversion to a tenure-track position upon successful completion of a doctorate degree, contingent upon department and institutional needs. The position will begin August 1, 2027.\u00a0This is a full-time, nine-month, non-tenure-track or tenure-track or position with a renewable annual contract. The selected candidate will have a demonstrated commitment to pursuing teaching excellence at Washburn University, including a dedication to developing inclusive teaching practices that engage all learners. The Washburn Biology Department offers degrees in the following majors: general biology, environmental biology, forensic biology, molecular biology & biotechnology, and biology secondary education. In addition, the department teaches several service courses that support programs in Nursing, Kinesiology, and Allied Health, among others. The successful candidate will be expected to collaborate pedagogically with a cohesive team of student-centered faculty. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: \u2022 Fulfill teaching expectations associated with lecturer or tenure-track appointment. Teach 12-faculty load hours per semester (either in-person or online, according to departmental needs) or equivalent full workload as outlined in the faculty handbook. \u2022 Teach and develop undergraduate classes as assigned and as dependent upon department needs, which may include introductory human biology lecture and lab, human anatomy, developmental biology, histology, in addition to other courses consistent with the candidate\u2019s training and interests. \u2022 For position as assistant professor only: Fulfill scholarship expectations associated with a tenure-track appointment. \u2022 Fulfill service expectations associated with lecturer or tenure-track appointment by engaging in service activities in the department, university, and profession. \u2022 Perform additional job-related duties as assigned or as appropriate. Required Qualifications: Required Qualifications for Lecturer (Non-tenure-track) Position: \u2022 Master\u2019s degree in anatomy, biology, or closely related field. \u2022 Demonstrated dedication to developing inclusive teaching practices that engage all learners. Required Qualifications for Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) Position: \u2022 Ph.D. in anatomy, biology, or closely related field. ABD applicants will be considered, with completion of the doctorate by August 1, 2028. \u2022 Demonstrated dedication to developing inclusive teaching practices that engage all learners. \u2022 Experience or potential for research in field of anatomy or related biology disciplines. \u2022 Official educational transcripts required by all faculty at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Experience teaching at the university level. \u2022 Teaching experience and course development in the areas of human anatomy. \u2022 Experience or potential for research in anatomy or related discipline. \u2022 Experience or potential to involve undergraduate students in research projects. Special Instructions to Applicants: \u2022 Please upload the following items as .pdf files to the \u201cadditional documents\u201d fields via the electronic application: a letter of interest, statement of teaching philosophy with inclusive teaching practices, evidence of teaching effectiveness (such as student or peer evaluations), and (for tenure-track position only) an outline of research plans, especially those involving undergraduates. Contact information for three current professional references will be collected as part of the application form. \u2022 If you have questions about the position, please contact Dr. Erica Jackson, Chair, Anatomy Biology Search Committee erica.jackson@washburn.edu . Please indicate \u201cANATOMY SEARCH\u201d in the email subject line. Application Deadline:\u00a0\u00a0Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants can be assured of full consideration if submitted by November 13, 2026. Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) 53e5a6dc Last Name (required) 919a7f1d Email (required) bc59be5b Job Alert aa172650 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments College of Arts & Sciences College of Arts & Sciences Categories Biology/Chemistry/Physics/Astronomy Biology/Chemistry/Physics/Astronomy Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Washburn University\u2019s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 901ba11d Last Name (required) 3c0a03d5 Email (required) 3c42c062 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking \u201cI Accept\u201d or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"}, "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/lecturer-clinical-coordinator-medical-dosimetry-topeka-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry)", "description": "Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Faculty Lecturer Position Title: Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) Department: Allied Health Campus Location: Washburn University Position Summary: Washburn University\u2019s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. The Allied Health Department at Washburn University offers nationally accredited programs and offerings at multiple levels including associate\u2019s, bachelor\u2019s, and master\u2019s degrees. Each selected candidate will have a demonstrated commitment to pursuing teaching excellence at Washburn University, including a dedication to developing inclusive teaching practices that engage all learners. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: \u2022 Teach 12 credit hours per semester or a full workload as defined by the faculty handbook. \u2022 Teach and develop didactic and/or clinical Allied Health Department courses, as appropriate, in assigned modalities. \u2022 Advise students, maintain office hours in accordance with SAS and university policy, attend meetings, and engage in service activities in the Allied Health Department, the School of Applied Studies, the University, the profession, and the community. \u2022 Correlate and coordinate clinical education with didactic education and evaluate its effectiveness. \u2022 Support the program director to ensure effective program operations. \u2022 Participate in the accreditation and assessment processes. \u2022 Maintain current knowledge of the professional discipline and educational methodologies through continuing professional development. \u2022 Maintain current knowledge of program policies, procedures, and student progress. \u2022 Must hold and maintain a valid Medical Dosimetrist Certification Board (MDCB) certification or equivalent. \u2022 If converted to a tenure track position, responsibilities will include scholarly activity. Required Qualifications: \u2022 A relevant master\u2019s degree from an academic institution accredited by an institutional accrediting agency recognized by the U.S. Department of Education (USDE). \u2022 Minimum of two years\u2019 clinical experience as a Certified Medical Dosimetrist (CMD). \u2022 Minimum of one year of experience as an instructor in a JRCERT-accredited program. \u2022 Experience in curriculum development, supervision, instruction, evaluation, and academic advising. \u2022 Current Medical Dosimetrist Certification Board (MDCB) certification. \u2022 Demonstrated dedication to developing inclusive teaching practices that engage all learners. \u2022 Official educational transcripts required at the time of hire. \u2022 Must hold and maintain a valid Medical Dosimetrist Certification Board (MDCB) certification. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 A relevant doctorate degree from an academic institution accredited by an institutional accrediting agency recognized by the U.S. Department of Education (USDE). \u2022 Experience in teaching online courses. \u2022 Effective organizational and interpersonal skills. Special Instructions to Applicants: Questions pertaining to this position may be directed to Allied Health department chair, Mark Kohls mark.kohls@washburn.edu. Application Deadline:\u00a0\u00a0Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants can be assured of full consideration if submitted by October 26, 2026. Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) 1991a120 Last Name (required) 3561b8f7 Email (required) 8bf2e063 Job Alert 66d8e290 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Applied Studies School of Applied Studies Categories Allied Health, Applied Studies, Education Allied Health, Applied Studies, Education Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. University Counselor / Campus Advocate (Two positions) Counseling Washburn University is accepting applications to hire two University Counselor / Campus Advocate positions. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) d6af3fb0 Last Name (required) 63e306ac Email (required) ac56221d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking \u201cI Accept\u201d or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"}, "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/maintenance-technician-four-positions-updated-7-7-20026-topeka-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Maintenance Technician (Four Positions) (Updated 7/7/20026)", "description": "Maintenance Technician (Four Positions) (Updated 7/7/20026) - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Maintenance Technician (Four Positions) (Updated 7/7/20026) Facilities Services Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Maintenance Technician (Four Positions) (Updated 7/7/20026) Facilities Services Staff Full-time Position Title: Maintenance Technician (Four Positions)\u00a0(Updated 7/7/20026) Department: Facilities Services (CBU) Advertised Pay: $20.60/hr Campus Location: Washburn University Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Position Summary: Under general supervision, the Maintenance Technician performs a variety of skilled and semi-skilled duties to ensure the proper functioning, safety, and operational efficiency of Washburn buildings, systems, and equipment. This role requires a proactive approach to maintenance, strong problem-solving skills, and collaboration with campus staff, contractors, and external partners. The Maintenance Technician is a vital member of the Facilities team, contributing to a well-maintained and safe environment for the entire Washburn community. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: HVAC, Boiler, and Mechanical Systems \u2022 Operate, monitor, and perform preventative and corrective maintenance on heating, ventilation, air conditioning (HVAC), and boiler systems. This includes tasks such as repairing boilers, pumps, and related support equipment, and checking building automation systems (BAS) for temperature and equipment functionality. General Building and System Maintenance \u2022 Perform skilled and semi-skilled repair work on building structures and mechanical systems as assigned through the Computerized Maintenance Management System (CMMS) or other software. \u2022 Inspect and address deficiencies in building systems, including plumbing, electrical, and HVAC equipment. \u2022 Maintain building interiors by repairing ceiling tiles, floor tile, cove bases, and other materials; patching and painting interior walls and surfaces; and replacing lamps. \u2022 Address plumbing issues, including clearing sewage blockages, drain lines, and cleaning roof drains. \u2022 Conduct repairs on doors, locks, and other hardware. Inspections and Diagnostics \u2022 Inspect and test various campus systems and equipment, including air compressors, fire sprinkler piping systems, grease traps, and sewer pumps, to ensure optimal function and safety. Facility Operations and Support \u2022 Provide essential service and event support across campus as directed by Facilities supervisors. \u2022 Perform snow and ice removal duties as assigned during inclement weather. \u2022 Conduct maintenance on water features, swimming pools, and/or whirlpools, including minor water chemical treatments, adhering to manufacturer guidelines and Washburn standards. Compliance and Reporting \u2022 Ensure all maintenance tasks are performed according to manufacturer specifications and Washburn, local, and OSHA safety regulations. \u2022 Document all completed repairs, work orders, and inspections accurately within the CMMS or other designated software. \u2022 Communicate deficiencies to immediate supervisors and recommend process improvements to enhance operational efficiency. Collaboration \u2022 Work with and assist engineers, contractors, and consultants during safety evaluations, system repairs, and project planning. Provide information on Washburn procedures and practices to support project coordination. Professional Conduct \u2022 Always maintain a professional, safe, and clean work environment. Perform additional job-related duties as assigned or as appropriate. Required Qualifications: \u2022 High school diploma, GED, or equivalent. \u2022 One year of relevant work experience in building maintenance, or completion of a certified trade program in a related field. \u2022 Demonstrated training in Building Maintenance, acquired through on-the-job training or a completed certification program. \u2022 Proven ability in maintaining commercial building mechanical systems. \u2022 Effective communication skills. \u2022 Demonstrated ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a team. \u2022 Demonstrated effective troubleshooting and problem-solving skills to diagnose and repair issues efficiently. \u2022 Valid driver\u2019s license with an acceptable driving record under Washburn standards. Physical Requirements: \u2022 The ability to move, lift, and maneuver materials weighing up to 50 pounds. Heavier items may require team lifting. \u2022 Ability to work from a ladder and/or lifts, safely. Training provided. \u2022 Must be able to respond to emergency service calls outside of regularly scheduled work hours and be available to work various shifts as assigned. \u2022 The role involves exposure to various physical hazards associated with building maintenance and repair, as well as outdoor weather conditions. \u2022 This is a Designated Safety Sensitive position and will be required to undergo drug screening. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Proven expertise in at least two different skilled trades relevant to building maintenance (e.g., electrical, plumbing, carpentry). \u2022 Experience with a Computerized Maintenance Management System (CMMS). \u2022 Experience with a Building Automation System (BAS). \u2022 Safety or chemical management training. \u2022 Fundamental computer literacy, including the ability to enter data and communicate via email. Special Instructions to Applicants: Hourly, Full-time, Mon-Fri, 8am-4:30pm Background check, driving history, and drug screen are required. Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) fe13c01a Last Name (required) ebae2528 Email (required) daacfa53 Job Alert 8647cd68 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Facilities Services Facilities Services Categories Facilities Maint/HVAC/Mgmt. Facilities Maint/HVAC/Mgmt. Send Please wait... 