r, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking \u201cI Accept\u201d or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"}, "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/office-coordinator-topeka-kansas-united-states-4cbd4189-a31c-4067-99fb-0cd2b6877113": {"title": "Office Coordinator", "description": "Office Coordinator - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Office Coordinator Human Resources Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Office Coordinator Human Resources Staff Full-time Position Title: Office Coordinator Department: Human Resources Advertised Pay: Base $18.54/hour with potential for a higher entry rate commensurate with experience Campus Location: Washburn University Application Review: Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Position Summary: This position is responsible for providing administrative support and coordination for Human Resources and is responsible for delivering prompt, accurate, and exemplary customer service to administrators, faculty, staff, students, applicants, and external constituents through multiple methods of communication. This position serves as a primary point of contact for the office and performs a wide variety of administrative, records management, compliance, and operational support functions with minimal supervision. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: \u2022 Serve as a point of contact for Human Resources by greeting visitors, answering incoming phone calls, and responding to inquiries or directing individuals to the appropriate office or staff member for assistance. Provide courteous and professional customer service, particularly when assisting individuals experiencing sensitive or urgent personnel-related matters. \u2022 Provide office coordination and administrative support for Human Resources operations, including scheduling meeting rooms, assisting with mail merges, maintaining office supplies, placing food orders, and supporting general office workflow and communications. \u2022 Facilitate the completion of employee and student Form I-9 processes by assisting individuals with understanding federal requirements, reviewing documentation, completing employer verification requirements, and ensuring forms are processed and retained accurately in accordance with federal regulations. \u2022 Process employment verifications, Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) employment certification requests, address changes, transcript requests, and other employment-related documentation in a timely and accurate manner. \u2022 Assist with imaging, scanning, indexing, retrieval, and correction of personnel and employment records within electronic document management systems, including personnel documents, performance evaluations, employment verifications, and new hire documentation. \u2022 Assist Talent Acquisition by transferring application materials from the applicant tracking system to personnel files, posting open positions to designated websites, organizing recruitment files for records retention, and supporting other recruitment-related administrative processes. \u2022 Maintain and update employee and applicant records within institutional systems, including updates related to certifications, verified credentials, background checks, motor vehicle records (MVR), and other employment compliance requirements. \u2022 Assist with Human Resources system maintenance and data cleanup activities, including student employee job terminations in Banner, inactivation of SIAINST records, and PEAEMPL record maintenance. \u2022 Prepare and submit required reports and documentation, including the Kansas Department of Labor bi-monthly report and other compliance-related reporting requirements. \u2022 Support Human Resources financial and administrative processes, including Concur-related administrative assistance and coordination of departmental documentation and forms. \u2022 Assist with maintaining and updating Human Resources forms, webpages, and online information to ensure materials are current, accurate, and appropriately accessible. \u2022 Perform additional job-related duties as assigned or as appropriate. Required Qualifications: \u2022 Bachelor\u2019s degree or a combination of post-secondary education and additional administrative support experience equivalent to a degree. \u2022 Demonstrated effective communication and customer service skills. \u2022 Proficient skills in proofreading and using Microsoft Word. \u2022 Proven ability to work with colleagues in a team-oriented environment and complete assignments independently. \u2022 Ability and willingness to learn and use new computer software. \u2022 Proven ability to maintain confidentiality in the workplace. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 At least one year of professional experience working in a Human Resources department. Special Instructions to Applicants: The interview process will require completing a skills assessment to determine candidates\u2019 proficiency in the software and skills needed to perform the position's essential functions. The information will be provided to selected candidates during the interview process. Hourly, Full-time, Mon-Fri, 8am-5pm Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) 9b4a7600 Last Name (required) 877cc412 Email (required) 5e2eed06 Job Alert fc6fc25c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Human Resources Human Resources Categories Human Resources/EEO/Title IX Human Resources/EEO/Title IX Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Washburn University\u2019s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 53c00cd6 Last Name (required) 8db9a153 Email (required) 202e6e87 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking \u201cI Accept\u201d or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"}, "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/police-officer-topeka-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Police Officer (Two Positions)", "description": "Police Officer (Two Positions) - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Police Officer (Two Positions) University Police Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Police Officer (Two Positions) University Police Staff Full-time Position Title: Police Officer\u00a0(Two Positions) Department: University Police Advertised Pay: $25.91/hr Campus Location: Washburn University Application Review: Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Position Summary: It is essential for the University Police Officer to maintain high visibility on campus as a deterrent to crime. The employee is required to carry a firearm when on duty. The use of computers and various computer software may be necessary to complete many of the following tasks. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: \u2022 Patrol the University campus on foot, on bicycle, or in a patrol car, watching for activities that violate city ordinance, state statute, federal law, or University policies. Intervene in illegal activity and restore order, investigate causative factors, determine and initiate the best course of action to resolve the problem(s). Make arrests when and where necessary. \u2022 Patrol campus streets, parking lots, and driveways to ensure the proper flow of traffic and control parking on campus. Take appropriate enforcement action when illegally parked vehicles are located. \u2022 Check the security of all buildings on campus to ensure they are locked or unlocked as scheduled for each building and to ensure that buildings and contents are secure and all security measures are intact. \u2022 Following the established format for daily log reports, produce written reports detailing daily activities. Produce detailed offense reports of any crime reported on campus, supplemental investigative reports to record any information gathered as the result of an investigation, arrest reports for prosecution, and affidavits for charges as required by the state and District Attorney. Produce accident reports detailing accident investigations as required by the Kansas Department of Transportation. Produce information reports for any other activities on campus. \u2022 Establish professional contact with the University community: Provide directions to buildings, events, and classes. Unlock vehicles for vehicle owners who have locked their keys inside. Escort students who have concerns for their safety to campus locations. Jump-start vehicles that will not start. Unlock buildings and classroom doors for students and faculty who are authorized to be inside. Present safety talks to groups and organizations as requested. \u2022 Attend in-service training to update knowledge and skills in police procedure, firearms proficiency, first aid, CPR, AED, and legal issues, and remain in compliance with the Kansas Commission on Peace Officers Standards and Training requirement for no less than 40 hours of in-service training each year. \u2022 Attend briefings with the supervisor(s) to receive instructions, daily briefing information, legal updates, schedule changes, performance evaluations, and general work-related information. \u2022 Perform additional job-related duties as assigned or appropriate. Required Qualifications: \u2022 High School Diploma, GED, or equivalent. \u2022 Ability to work any shift/hours as assigned and to respond to emergency call-back in a reasonable amount of time. Proficiency using desktop, Windows-based computer operating systems and proven ability to learn and adapt to the use of new computer software. \u2022 Demonstrated proficiency in the use of firearms. \u2022 Must be able to successfully pass a written examination, physical agility test, polygraph examination, psychological examination, drug testing examination, and verbal interview. \u2022 Valid Class C Driver\u2019s License with an acceptable driving record under University standards. \u2022 Certification from the Kansas Commission on Peace Officers Standards and Training as mandated by state law. Physical Requirements: \u2022 This is a \u201cdesignated safety-sensitive position\u201d and will be required to undergo drug testing. \u2022 Per Kansas Statute 74-5605, each applicant for certification shall meet the following minimum requirements: (1) Be a United States citizen; (2) have been fingerprinted and a search of local, state, and national fingerprint files made to determine whether the applicant has a criminal record; (3) not have been convicted of a crime that would constitute a felony under the laws of this state, a misdemeanor crime of domestic violence, or a misdemeanor offense that the commission determines reflects on the honesty, trustworthiness, integrity, or competence of the applicant as defined by rules and regulations of the commission; (4) have: (A) graduated from a high school accredited by the Kansas state board of education or the appropriate accrediting agency of another state jurisdiction; (B) obtained a high school education from a nonaccredited private secondary school as defined in K.S.A. 72-4345, and amendments thereto; or \u00a9 obtained the equivalent of a high school education as defined by rules and regulations of the commission; (5) be of good moral character sufficient to warrant the public trust in the applicant as a police officer or law enforcement officer; (6) have completed an assessment, including psychological testing approved by the commission, to determine that the applicant does not have a mental or personality disorder that would adversely affect the ability to perform the essential functions of a police officer or law enforcement officer with reasonable skill, safety, and judgment; (7) be free of any physical or mental condition which adversely affects the ability to perform the essential functions of a police officer or law enforcement officer with reasonable skill, safety, and judgment; and (8) be at least 21 years of age. \u2022 No arrests for domestic violence, stalking, dating violence, or any classification of these crimes. No convictions for any felony crime. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Completion of college coursework in the criminal justice field. \u2022 Independent leadership experience. Hourly, Full-time Background check, driving history, and drug screen are required. Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) e476c1d3 Last Name (required) 30812732 Email (required) 2996f042 Job Alert c747994a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments University Police University Police Categories Police and Public Safety Police and Public Safety Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school students through partner districts. Student Involvement and Development Manager Student Involvement & Development Washburn University is accepting applications for a Student Involvement and Development Manager. Senior Custodian Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Lecturer/Clinical Coordinator (Medical Dosimetry) School of Applied Studies Washburn University\u2019s Allied Health Department invites applications for the position of Medical Dosimetry Clinical Coordinator/Lecturer with a start date of January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. This position is a 12-month full-time, lecturer faculty appointment with possible conversion to tenure track. Application Analyst Information Technology Services Washburn University is accepting applications for an Application Analyst. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 67179bb6 Last Name (required) 404ad803 Email (required) c4a85a94 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking \u201cI Accept\u201d or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"}, "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/senior-administrative-specialist-topeka-kansas-united-states-7bd61c9c-49eb-47b6-8a3f-647c8848459b": {"title": "Senior Administrative Specialist", "description": "Senior Administrative Specialist - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Senior Administrative Specialist Aleshire Center for Leadership and Community Engagement Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Senior Administrative Specialist Aleshire Center for Leadership and Community Engagement Staff Full-time Position Title: Senior Administrative Specialist Department: Aleshire Ctr for Leadership & Comm Advertised Pay: Base $16.85/hour with potential for a higher entry rate commensurate with experience Campus Location: Washburn University Application Review: Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Position Summary: The Senior Administrative Specialist provides administrative support to the Aleshire Center for Leadership and Community Engagement. The employee must maintain the confidentiality of all privileged/sensitive information. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For\u00ae program. Essential Functions: \u2022 Serve as primary receptionist: greeting and directing visitors, answering telephones, transferring calls, and/or taking and relaying messages. Monitor and review all incoming email messages to the departmental email account, responding to inquiries and requests as appropriate or forwarding/referring messages for response as appropriate, confirming responses as needed. Distribute office mail. Maintain the supply of office supplies for the Aleshire Center's use. Monitor the use and function of office equipment, assisting users with equipment operation, planning for repairs and maintenance as necessary. Update website as needed and submit Aleshire Center events to the Washburn calendar. Draft and format correspondence, reports, etc. as directed. Record, type, and distribute meeting notes as requested. Update email list and email listserv each semester to have the most accurate list of students involved in the Aleshire Center to receive information on activities of the Aleshire Center. Inventory, organize, and track the use of items in the storage room to better utilize the resources available. \u2022 Serve as primary support for the recruitment efforts of the Aleshire Center by providing communications through email, social media, and printed promotions. Track students that are interested in programs of the Aleshire Center for outreach. Provide support for the Learning Community, including preparing materials and mailings for recruitment of students to participate, tracking student participation in Aleshire Center activities, and acting as a resource for the Learning Community RA. Prepare materials for scholarship recruitment, provide email and mailings for schools for scholarship promotions. Provide logistics for Scholarship Interview Day. Provide support for the Aleshire Center at NSO\u2019s and other Admissions events by preparing needed materials, organizing student involvement, and being available to give presentations or table as needed. \u2022 Track students involved in the Aleshire Center through Banner coding each semester. Promote Leadership Studies and Community Studies courses to current Washburn students who have completed prerequisite courses. Determine the continued scholarship eligibility of students receiving Aleshire Center scholarships according to the current Scholarship Acceptance Form. \u2022 Assist with semester planning and preparations for Leadership Studies, Community Studies, and MACNLE courses: Enter class schedules into Banner, coordinate adjunct instructors and contracts using FLAC, compile information from faculty and submit textbook adoptions, and order instructor textbooks. \u2022 Provide support for the Leadership Washburn Transformational Experience and Community & Civic Engagement Washburn Transformational Experience. Track students who have declared a WTE through coursework and project management. Provide information for the recognition of students. Produce and update WTE materials for promotion through the Aleshire Center as needed. \u2022 Provide primary assistance for student event coordination efforts, as directed, including but not limited to Scholarship Interview Day, end-of-year celebrations, Leaders of Tomorrow activities, and other All-Center events. Prepare and distribute promotional materials to fully publicize Aleshire Center events. Schedule student meetings and activities/events on Aleshire Center faculty and staff calendars as needed. \u2022 Advise and direct students throughout major events to provide support and a learning experience. As needed, schedule student meetings; locate and reserve meeting space; arrange for refreshments or catering; contact and invite participants; develop, type, copy, and distribute meeting materials, if needed; and guide students to consider and prepare for all details in preparation for meetings and activities. Review and assess completed events to identify opportunities for change and improvement for future events. \u2022 Establish and maintain files to document students\u2019 attendance and activities for reference and reporting purposes. \u2022 Assist with the Washburn Leadership Challenge Event\u00ae by taking the lead on promotion to schools, team registration, participant information, including waivers, hotel rooming assignments, and food orders. Complete other WLCE\u00ae tasks as requested. \u2022 Provide support for the Aleshire Center Advisory Board, including setting dates, reserving rooms, gathering RSVP\u2019s, ordering lunch, providing materials as needed, tracking RSVP, setting up technology, and meeting other needs as they arise. Record, type, copy, and distribute meeting notes. Update Advisory Board contact information. \u2022 Perform additional job-related duties as assigned or as appropriate. Required Qualifications: \u2022 High School diploma, GED, or equivalent. \u2022 One year of full-time relevant work experience or post-secondary education or a combination equal to one year. \u2022 Demonstrated effective interpersonal, communication, analytical, critical thinking, organizational, and time management skills. \u2022 Proven proficiency with Microsoft 365 programs, including Outlook, Word, Excel, and Teams, with the capacity to learn key functions in essential software. \u2022 Demonstrated ability to work effectively individually and collaboratively as part of a team. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Successful completion of college coursework. \u2022 Previous related experience in a higher education environment. Special Instructions to Applicants: Hourly, Full-time, Mon-Fri, 8am-5pm Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) 803d9d03 Last Name (required) 9ac4d2d4 Email (required) 4bf2ee52 Job Alert c5b7799e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Aleshire Center for Leadership and Community Engagement Aleshire Center for Leadership and Community Engagement Categories Admin Support, Exec Assistants Admin Support, Exec Assistants Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Technical Instructor (Life Sciences) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology is seeking applications for Life Sciences Technical Instructor. This 12-month instructor position is full-time and benefit eligible. An anticipated hire date is as soon as November 1, 2026 but negotiable. Work schedule is M-F 7:30 am \u2013 4:30 pm. Director, Student Affairs WIT-Administration Washburn University's Division of Student Life seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Student Life for the Washburn Institute of Technology (Washburn Tech). This role is the lead student affairs professional on the Washburn Tech campuses, where technical education serves both adult learners and high school s